#Work in progress

Dev: NoahGNielsen

Setup
-----
1. Upload the contents of src/ to the web root (the GitHub workflow does this to hbhub/ on every push to main).
2. Copy config-examples/hbHubSiteConfig.example.php into the folder one level ABOVE the web root,
   rename it to hbHubSiteConfig.php, and fill in the values. The site only looks for it there.
   For local development with src/ as the web root, that means the repo root (it's in .gitignore).
3. Create the database tables by importing database/schema.sql (e.g. in phpMyAdmin).

Folders
-------
src/              The website itself (everything here gets uploaded)
config-examples/  Templates for config files that live outside the web root
database/         Database schema and default values (database/defaultUserSettings.json is the
                  default for the userSettings column in HBHub-Users)
